olks have been asking  in the Q&amp;A box if you could share  something like a piece of advice either  with applicant you or like MBA one year  you when you were just starting what  would that advice be yeah for MBA one me  I would say that if you haven't heard  already there there is this notion of  the FOMO or fear of missing out there  are going to be a lot of events going on  on campus  you got your classwork you got these  career events you have clubs and then  you have just the natural tendency  of classmates just wanted to hang out  grab a drink or go for a walk or whatnot  and it can very easily overwhelm you  very quickly and the thing is it's just  treated like you've treated anything  else in the past it's something that you  know it's okay to say no to certain  events it's okay to take certain time  there's not this notion that everyone's  doing something at any given time like  it is okay to like you know this is your  journey so you know make sure you take  time to to do what you want to do and if  you need some time off you know to make  sure you do that it in make this  experience how you want this experience  to be  [Music]

